"Tonieplay game card not recognised – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-gb/articles/29537628346770-Tonieplay-game-card-not-recognised)\nciteturn778search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # Tonieplay game card not recognised\n\n# Tonieplay game card not recognised\n\nWe’re sorry to hear you’re having trouble with your Tonieplay game cards! Don’t worry - we’ll help you get back on track.\n\nSometimes a simple restart solves the issue:\n\n  1. Make sure your Toniebox 2 is on and unplugged.\n  2. Squeeze both ears until the Toniebox enters the sleep light with timer setting.\n  3. Keep squeezing until it restarts (this can take 20-60 seconds).\n  4. You’ll know it worked when you see the Welcome Lights show.\n\nOnce your Toniebox 2 has restarted, wait a minute before trying your Tonieplay game again. \n\nIf the issue continues, try a factory reset:\n\n  1. Turn on your Toniebox 2 and wait for the light ring to turn green.\n  2. Ensure it is not plugged in to power.\n  3. Turn it upside down and press both ears for 5 seconds until you hear a sound signal.\n  4. Turn it back upright - the light ring will glow white.\n  5. Press and hold the small ear to start the reset.\n  6. Follow the prompts until the Toniebox 2 confirms the reset is complete.\n\n \n\nStill having trouble?\nIf none of these steps work, please let us know. We’ll make sure your little one is back to playing in no time!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow long does the Toniebox 2 remember your auto-saved status when you remove the disc, take a break or play something else? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/articles/29036389045778-How-long-does-the-Toniebox-2-remember-your-auto-saved-status-when-you-remove-the-disc-take-a-break-or-play-something-else)\nciteturn778search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # How long does the Toniebox 2 remember your auto-saved status when you remove the disc, take a break or play something else?\n\n# How long does the Toniebox 2 remember your auto-saved status when you remove the disc, take a break or play something else?\n\nIf you remove your Tonieplay disc for a break or to play another Tonie product, the progress will stop. This means that the game is not \"paused\" anymore, but you will load it up from scratch again. \nHowever, each game acts a little differently. For example the quiz games will not continue a running round of let's say 5 questions. An interactive story will be resumable at the last position. A Discover Game will start a new \"round\".--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTonieplay - Troubleshooting Tips – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-gb/articles/29255022702354-Tonieplay-Troubleshooting-Tips)\nciteturn778search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Let's take a look at some of the most common Tonieplay troubleshooting tips, to get your adventure off to a great start! ... If you experience further issues, reach out to our Customer Happiness team and we’ll be able to support you further.\n\n# Tonieplay - Troubleshooting Tips\n\nImage\n\nLet's take a look at some of the most common Tonieplay troubleshooting tips, to get your adventure off to a great start!\n\nTonieplay game taking too long to download\n\nWhen you place a Tonieplay game on your Toniebox 2 for the very first time, it needs to download the game before the fun can begin. This usually takes up to 30 minutes, but depending on the size of the game and your Wi-Fi speed this could take an hour or more. \n\nNote that our longer games, like Quizzles, will take the longest time to download.\n\nWhile you wait, keep an eye on the green progress bar on the Dynamic Light Ring – that’s your Toniebox 2 showing you how far along the download is. As soon as it’s complete, your game will start automatically. Next time you play, it will begin right away, even without Wi-Fi – just like a regular Tonie.\n\nIf the download doesn’t seem to be moving along and your Toniebox 2 feels a little “stuck,” simply remove the game disc, restart the Toniebox 2, and try again.\n\nTonieplay disc not detected\n\nThe Tonieplay Discs are really strong and will likely be detected as you’re placing them on top of your Toniebox 2.\n\nIf you do have issues, please check that the disc is pressed down onto the top of the Toniebox 2 correctly.\n\nIf you continue to experience issues, take the Tonieplay disc off, reset your Toniebox 2 and try again.\n\nIf you experience further issues, reach out to our Customer Happiness team and we’ll be able to support you further.\n\nThe Light Ring is stuck flashing white\n\nIf your Toniebox 2 Light Ring keeps flashing white during a play session, all you need to do is remove both the Tonieplay disc and Tonieplay Controller from the Toniebox 2, wait a moment before replacing both and then start again!\n\nTonieplay Not Recognised\n\nIf your Tonieplay disc is not recognised by the Toniebox 2, try the following steps:\n\nWait a moment – Sometimes the Toniebox 2 just needs a little time to catch up and download any necessary updates or content.\n\nRestart the Toniebox 2 – If the disc is still not recognised, restart the device and try again.\n\nFactory reset – If the issue persists, perform a full factory reset on your Toniebox 2 and then try using the Tonieplay disc again.\n\nTonieplay game card not recognised\n\nWe’re sorry to hear you’re having trouble with your Tonieplay game cards! Don’t worry - we’ll help you get back on track.\n\nSometimes a simple restart solves the issue:\n\n  * Make sure your Toniebox 2 is on and unplugged.\n  * Squeeze both ears until the Toniebox enters the sleep light with timer setting.\n  * Keep squeezing until it restarts (this can take 20-60 seconds).\n  * You’ll know it worked when you see the Welcome Lights show.\n\nOnce your Toniebox 2 has restarted, wait a minute before trying your Tonieplay game again.\n\nIf the issue continues, try a factory reset:\n\n  * Turn on your Toniebox 2 and wait for the light ring to turn green.\n  * Ensure it is not plugged in to power.\n  * Turn it upside down and press both ears for 5 seconds until you hear a sound signal.\n  * Turn it back upright - the light ring will glow white.\n  * Press and hold the small ear to start the reset.\n  * Follow the prompts until the Toniebox 2 confirms the reset is complete.\n\nIf you have any other issues with , send us a message and we will be there to help!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTonieplay – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-150/sections/29036400009490-Tonieplay)\nciteturn778search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; ### Tonieplay - Troubleshooting Tips\n\n# Tonieplay\n\n### Popular Articles\n\n## Articles\n\n14 articles\n\n### What is Tonieplay?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Tonieplay - Troubleshooting Tips\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Tonieplay game card not recognised\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How long does the Toniebox 2 remember your auto-saved status when you remove the disc, take a break or play something else?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Can you ever choose the chapter?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Can I restart a Tonieplay game?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### What do I need in order to play a Tonieplay game?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### What aged children is Tonieplay suitable for?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Is Tonieplay compatible with Toniebox 1?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Are Tonieplay games multiplayer?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How much help will my child need with playing a Tonieplay game?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### Can I skip past the intro to the Tonieplay game?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How do Tonieplay games appear in the app?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### What new Tonieplay specific data will we capture?\n\nRead Full Article →--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTonieplay – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-gb/sections/29036400009490-Tonieplay)\nciteturn778search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Let's take a look at some of the most common Tonieplay troubleshooting tips, to get your adventure off to a great start! ... Just like with all our other Tonies, once you’ve put a Tonieplay Game on the Toniebox 2 you’ll be able to see it in the ‘Mine’ section of the app.\n\n# Tonieplay\n\n### Popular Articles\n\nTonieplay\n\nBrowse Topic\n\nQuick Search\n\n[Input: Search for articles, guides, and help...]\n\n## Articles\n\n14 articles\n\n### What is Tonieplay?\n\nLet the listening journey continue! Designed especially for Toniebox 2, Tonieplay turns the Toniebox into a safe and screen-free gaming experience. You’ll need a Tonieplay controller to play any of our amazing Tonieplay games – both are sold separately.\n\n### Tonieplay - Troubleshooting Tips\n\nLet's take a look at some of the most common Tonieplay troubleshooting tips, to get your adventure off to a great start! Tonieplay game taking too long to download When you place a Tonieplay game on your Toniebox 2 for the very first time, it needs to download the game before the fun can begin. This...\n\n### Tonieplay game card not recognised\n\nWe’re sorry to hear you’re having trouble with your Tonieplay game cards! Don’t worry - we’ll help you get back on track. Sometimes a simple restart solves the issue: Make sure your Toniebox 2 is on and unplugged. Squeeze both ears until the Toniebox enters the sleep light with timer setting. Keep s...\n\n### How long does the Toniebox 2 remember your auto-saved status when you remove the disc, take a break or play something else?\n\nIf you remove your Tonieplay disc for a break or to play another Tonie product, the progress will stop. This means that the game is not \"paused\" anymore, but you will load it up from scratch again. However, each game acts a little differently. For example the quiz games will not continue a running r...\n\n### Can you ever choose the chapter?\n\nThat highly depends on the games, but in most cases: no. The only game that lets you choose which story to play is Winnie The Pooh.\n\n### Can I restart a Tonieplay game?\n\nNeed to go back a bit in your game? Easy! Simply lift the Tonieplay Disc off your Toniebox 2, count to five (a little dramatic pause never hurt anyone ✨), and pop it back on. Your game will restart from the top, or depending on the Tonieplay game, will pick up at your most recent checkpoint, if you'...\n\n### What do I need in order to play a Tonieplay game?\n\nTo play a Tonieplay Game you’ll need a Toniebox 2 and a Tonieplay Controller. If it’s the first time the game is being played you’ll also need a WiFi connection, but after this it will work offline too.\n\n### What aged children is Tonieplay suitable for?\n\nThere are Tonieplay games for everyone from 3 years and up, with even more coming soon...\n\n### Is Tonieplay compatible with Toniebox 1?\n\nNo, due to the technological advancements of Tonieplay, it’s only compatible with our newest model, the Toniebox 2.\n\n### Are Tonieplay games multiplayer?\n\nGreat question! Yes! Although our Tonieplay Games are designed for solo play, they can all also be enjoyed together with friends or family.\n\n### How much help will my child need with playing a Tonieplay game?\n\nJust like with classic board games, we recommend parents join in for the first few rounds to help kids get started. Tonieplay Games are designed to be easy to follow, but we’ve also included a written manual in every box for those who prefer to read up first. Younger players may need a little suppor...\n\n### Can I skip past the intro to the Tonieplay game?\n\nYes! Most games include a skip feature so you can move forward or back through the story. Intros are usually skippable, but some moments – like answering a quiz question or making a choice in an interactive story – can’t be replayed right away.\n\n### How do Tonieplay games appear in the app?\n\nJust like with all our other Tonies, once you’ve put a Tonieplay Game on the Toniebox 2 you’ll be able to see it in the ‘Mine’ section of the app.\n\n### What new Tonieplay specific data will we capture?\n\nWhen you use the new function Tonieplay, usage and operation information about the in-game interaction with the Toniebox will be collected. We process the data (e.g. frequency of use of individual games, errors that resulted in termination of use) for the same purpose as we process all other Interac...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTroubleshooting – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-us/sections/29258108517522-Troubleshooting)\nciteturn778search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Give it a quick restart by following the simple steps in this guide: How to Restart Your Toniebox 2 ... If the Toniebox 2 starts playing audio from another Tonie, don’t worry—your little one has likely just swapped their Tonies too quickly. ... Before your story, song, or audio adventure can begin, the Toniebox 2 needs to download the opening chapter from our servers or the full game for a Tonieplay Disc.\n\n# Troubleshooting\n\n### Popular Articles\n\nTroubleshooting\n\n## Articles\n\n10 articles\n\n### How do I restart the Toniebox 2?\n\nIt doesn’t happen often, but if the Toniebox 2 isn’t doing what it’s supposed to, restarting it is the best way to get it back on track. No worries, it's simple to do: Make sure the Toniebox 2 is not plugged in. Squeeze both ears until the Toniebox 2 enters the sleep light with timer setting. Keep s...\n\n### How to reset your Toniebox 2 to factory settings\n\nThink of a factory reset as your Toniebox 2 “fresh start button.” It wipes everything clean and takes your Toniebox 2 back to the way it was on day one. Because it’s such a big step, a factory reset should only be used as a last resort, after you’ve tried all other troubleshooting tips. When to use ...\n\n### My Toniebox 2 is stuck, what do I do?\n\nOh no! Has your Toniebox 2 paused mid-adventure? Don’t worry, it’s an easy fix! Give it a quick restart by following the simple steps in this guide: How to Restart Your Toniebox 2\n\n### What can I do if my Toniebox 2 isn’t turning on?\n\nIf giving it a good old telling off hasn’t worked (we assume you’ve tried), then here are some suggestions of where to go next: You might need to restart your Toniebox. Here’s a little guide to walk you through it. If that doesn’t fix it, try giving your Toniebox a full recharge. It takes about 4 ho...\n\n### Why does my Toniebox 2 not play a Tonie when it is plugged in?\n\nThis is expected behaviour when your Toniebox 2 is set to 1+ mode. If you want to change this setting, simply open the tonies® app, tap on your Toniebox 2, select settings and the scroll to \"Age Mode\" to change from 1+ to 3+.\n\n### My Tonie isn't playing\n\nSome Toniebox 2 customers have had trouble downloading Tonies recently. The issue has now been fixed, but you’ll need to update your Toniebox 2 to make sure everything runs smoothly. Here’s how to do it: Switch on your Toniebox 2. Wait until it turns off again by itself. Switch it back on. Wait for ...\n\n### Tonie is playing the audio from a different Tonie\n\nIf the Toniebox 2 starts playing audio from another Tonie, don’t worry—your little one has likely just swapped their Tonies too quickly. This is an easy fix: simply remove the Tonie from the Toniebox 2, wait a few seconds, and then place the desired Tonie back on top to resume the listening fun.\n\n### Toniebox 2 download speed seems slow\n\nWhen you place a new Tonie or Tonieplay Disc on your Toniebox 2, the fun doesn’t always start instantly. Before your story, song, or audio adventure can begin, the Toniebox 2 needs to download the opening chapter from our servers or the full game for a Tonieplay Disc. What to expect: Tonies - Normal...\n\n### Tapping the Toniebox 2 to skip forward and back isn't working\n\nIf your Toniebox 2 isn’t skipping tracks when you give it a tap, don’t worry—it may just need to turn off and back on again. Your Toniebox 2 will turn off automatically on its own after five minutes of no activity. When it wakes up again, the tapping magic should be back in action.\n\n### My Tonie/Creative Tonie is not playing the updated content on the Toniebox 2\n\nIf you have edited the audio content on your Tonie or Creative Tonie but your Toniebox 2 is still playing the old content, there are two possible reasons for this: Your Toniebox 2 isn’t connected to Wi-Fi: Check whether your Toniebox 2 is connected to Wi-Fi. To do this, open the tonies app and tap o...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTonieplay – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-au/sections/29036400009490-Tonieplay)\nciteturn778search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Let's take a look at some of the most common Tonieplay troubleshooting tips, to get your adventure off to a great start! ... Just like with all our other Tonies, once you’ve put a Tonieplay Game on the Toniebox 2 you’ll be able to see it in the ‘Mine’ section of the app.\n\n# Tonieplay\n\n## Articles\n\n14 articles\n\n### What is Tonieplay?\n\nLet the listening journey continue! Designed especially for Toniebox 2, Tonieplay turns the Toniebox into a safe and screen-free gaming experience. You’ll need a Tonieplay controller to play any of our amazing Tonieplay games – both are sold separately.\n\n### Tonieplay - Troubleshooting Tips\n\nLet's take a look at some of the most common Tonieplay troubleshooting tips, to get your adventure off to a great start! Tonieplay game taking too long to download When you place a Tonieplay game on your Toniebox 2 for the very first time, it needs to download the game before the fun can begin. This...\n\n### Tonieplay game card not recognised\n\nWe’re sorry to hear you’re having trouble with your Tonieplay game cards! Don